This solution defines a helper function `is_prime(n)` to check if a given integer `n` is prime. It first checks the trivial cases of `n <= 1` and `n == 2`, then checks if `n` is divisible by 2. If it is, `n` is not prime. If not, it checks divisibility up to the square root of `n`, as any factors larger than that would have a corresponding factor smaller than the square root. The `prime_length(string)` function simply calls `is_prime(len(string))` to check if the length of the string is prime.

